-- TrailerCargo_Fixups: GENERATED by build/extract_fixups.py, do not edit.
--
-- The rotation each model needs so a cargo model lands the way vanilla lays
-- the same item on the ground. A dropped item is drawn through
-- `ItemModelRenderer.init` (:477-493), which applies rotateXYZ(0, pi, pi/2)
-- when the item is drawn from its WeaponSprite, then the inverse of the
-- model script's `attachment world`. A vehicle sub-model gets none of that,
-- so a model authored for it arrives turned: a plank stood on its end in
-- game on 2026-09-22.
--
-- Each entry is that composite rotation as XYZ Euler degrees, in the
-- engine's own convention (rotateXYZ = Rx Ry Rz), followed by the
-- attachment's `offset`: vanilla translates the mesh by minus that offset
-- before the rotation; the bounds table was measured with it, so the
-- render has to shift the model by the same amount or a leaf rake draws
-- half a tile ahead of its footprint (2026-09-23, heads through the
-- headboard). TrailerCargo_Bed.pose composes rotation and shift with the
-- item's yaw then writes the model's `rotate` and moves its `offset`.
--
-- 531 entries, from 545 model scripts with an `attachment world` plus 364
-- models the weapon-sprite fallback can reach. Models with neither - most
-- world item models, `GasCan_Ground`, `Log` - need no entry.
